
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Pronouns.mgr - Spanish-pack first/second-person pronouns (Phase 8).
#
# Spanish has a tú (informal) vs usted (formal) split that pairs naturally
# with the two-tier formality intent-tag scheme (untagged = tú, deferential
# = usted). Both bind to ?_you - the .ms2 rule layer doesn't distinguish them.
#
# v1 ships:
#   yo / mí / mi   - first-person (singular). mi is the possessive determiner.
#                    Plural (nosotros, nuestro) is a follow-up.
#   tú / ti / tu   - second-person informal singular.
#   usted / su     - second-person formal singular.
#   él / ella      - third-person; covered in NounPhrases via PNAME / REG_NP
#                    so not strictly needed here.
#
# Possessive forms in Spanish AGREE in number (mi/mis, tu/tus, su/sus) and
# in some cases gender (nuestro/nuestra). v1 emits singular forms only;
# plurals would need agreement consulted at realize time - same shared hook
# as Swedish adjective agreement (deferred).
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

:PRONOUN

"yo"     ?_I     .
"mí"     ?_I     .
"mi"     ?_I     .

"tú"     ?_you   .
"ti"     ?_you   .
"tu"     ?_you   .
"usted"  ?_you   .
"su"     ?_you   .

"este"   ?_this  .
"esto"   ?_this  .
"eso"    ?_this  .
